WEBVTT

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:07.480
Hakumei! Thanks for waiting!

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:12.490
Hey! Did you finally finish your work at the food stand, Mikochi?

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:14.360
By some miracle.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:17.990
Your pear jam at the Mujina store
is pretty popular, after all.

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:18.990
We were swamped. I thought that I'd be peeling pears forever...

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:20.830
One please.

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:22.210
Sure thing!

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:23.460
We were swamped. I thought that I'd be peeling pears forever...

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.000
Great work.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.710
What counts is that you made it in time.

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:31.010
They're right about to announce this year's songstress.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:36.010
The results of the voting have arrived!

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:39.140
This year's splendiferous songstress is...

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:41.640
Entry number 14:

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:46.810
Konju!

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:49.570
...who tied with one other entry.

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:50.650
What?!

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:53.490
A write-in candidate:

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:56.660
Mikochi!

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:58.370
These two songstresses will delight us with their song of celebration at the market square tomorrow!

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:02.660
No... wait... What?

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:04.160
These two songstresses will delight us with their song of celebration at the market square tomorrow!

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:09.170
I'm happy for you, Mikochi!

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:10.670
There's nothing to be happy about!

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:13.550
Really? You're a songstress, though.

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:16.130
Why should I be happy about that?

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:59.070
How on earth did this happen?

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:03.410
Your singing's earned you quite the reputation.

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:05.030
How, exactly?

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:10.080
See, you sing a lot whenever you're doing chores or taking your bath, right?

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:13.460
Um... Okay, go on...

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:18.210
That's why people come deliver the paper or sell stuff even if we're not on their route.

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:19.920
You didn't know?

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:21.800
I had no idea.

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:26.140
Anyway, I've never heard of there ever being <i>two</i> songstresses!

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:28.850
I just hope this is all one big mistake.

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:30.440
Oh, same here.

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:33.560
You're that girl from before.

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:37.650
I'm Konju, the minstrel. I'm this year's songstress.

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:43.950
The results were vexing, but there's
nothing to be done about it now.

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:46.410
Mikochi! Just don't weigh me dow—

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:49.750
Oh, don't worry. I'm withdrawing, anyway.

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:50.710
What?

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:54.000
Really? That's such a waste, Mikochi.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:58.170
I'm fine with that. Singing in front of people is embarrassing.

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:01.220
I never asked for the job in the first place.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:07.970
I'm delighted to hear of your withdrawal.

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:12.480
Please look forward to tomorrow's performance!

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:20.110
She seemed kind of... angry, huh?

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:22.490
Well, yeah, I guess she would be.

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:25.820
What? Are you trying to get me up on stage, too?

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:28.780
Nope. I'm not going to force you, but...

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:36.830
All right. Come with me to the mimosa tree right outside town.

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:40.460
We'll get a good view from there.

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:48.260
What are those things?

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:50.640
The tsukumogami.

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:57.020
Originally, the reason for holding this harvest festival was to give praise to the spirits of ancient tools.

00:04:57.020 --> 00:05:01.980
That's been long forgotten by now.
Today, we just celebrate the harvest.

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:06.740
But even now, they come gather to hear the songstress.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:09.620
I didn't know the song had that kind of meaning.

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:14.410
So that's why Konju was so angry, huh?

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:16.290
<i>I kinda doubt that.</i>

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:20.130
So what are you going to do, Songstress?

00:05:32.470 --> 00:05:36.140
You'd better not let me catch you smirking from the audience.

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:40.400
No promises! I've never been able to pull off a serious face.

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:53.830
Why are you even here?

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:58.580
You're pulling out, aren't you?

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:01.590
A-Are you okay, Konju?

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:07.090
Your face is beet red. It's gotta be a cold.

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:09.050
Can you sing?

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:13.100
Of course I can! Why, just last night...

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:18.480
I spent two hours vocalizing after getting out of the bath.

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:19.190
Stupid.

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:21.110
That's why, then.

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:23.860
Who asked you to butt into my business, anyway?!

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:27.360
This is pear jam from the Mujina store.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:30.360
It'll do your throat good,
so eat it before it's time to sing.

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:38.910
Where can I get a fresh towel?

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:40.540
You're not stopping me?

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:42.210
Do you want us to?

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:46.880
I suppose you won't be able to hit the high notes,

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:48.340
but can you sing?

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:56.640
My lyre and seductive alto are what people come to listen to.

00:06:57.430 --> 00:06:59.560
Then that's perfect.

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:02.150
<i>My</i> selling point is my soprano.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:07.990
Mikochi, don't weigh me down, okay?

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:10.820
That's my line, Konju.

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:16.410
Sorry to keep you waiting, everyone!

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:22.670
This year, I'll introduce you to our <i>two</i> extraordinary songstresses!

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:26.840
Konju and Mikochi!

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:20.810
<i>They gave a performance oozing with good cheer.</i>

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:27.150
A freshly-made smoked cheese quiche,

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:30.900
sockeye salmon wrapped in magnolia leaves
sockeye salmon wrapped in magnolia leaves

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:34.820
Look, the whole world is rejoicing

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:39.620
It's itching to dance with us

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:43.620
And what drink might fit a night like this?

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:47.590
How about something botanical with pepper in it?

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:52.840
We could even catch the moon with our tiny hands

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:54.470
At least, that's how we're feeling

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:56.430
Whoa... They're all so lively...
At least, that's how we're feeling

00:08:56.430 --> 00:08:57.930
Whoa... They're all so lively...

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:03.140
<i>It seems even the tsukumogami couldn't help but join in.</i>

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:08.900
What do we do about this?

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:12.740
Well, they'll probably come home when they're tired of playing.

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:26.000
The fish just aren't biting today.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:29.380
Hey, Hakumei, let's go home already.

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:31.170
Huh? What's up?

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:36.430
Recently, there's been a rumor about a fish spirit around here.

00:09:37.050 --> 00:09:39.890
It's okay. I've got soy sauce.

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:41.930
You're planning on eating a ghost?

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:55.690
Doesn't really seem like something I can eat...

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:58.030
Hey!

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:01.490
Mikochi, are you okay?

00:10:01.490 --> 00:10:03.120
H-Hey!

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:07.250
Sorry about that. It appears that my little one scared you.

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:11.460
Bring that girl along. I'll tend to her at my home.

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:19.130
Have you come to?

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:22.850
Where am I?

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:25.270
This is my laboratory.

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:29.650
My name is Sen. It is a pleasure.

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:33.230
Um, I was with my friend...

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:33.770
Yes.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:38.320
Outside the window?

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:43.280
Oh, Mikochi!

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:46.950
This turtle is amazing!
It's a sack of bones, but it's alive!

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:49.210
Don't keep that up too long.

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:51.670
George isn't too fond of ruckus.

00:10:51.670 --> 00:10:53.040
'Kay.

00:10:54.710 --> 00:10:57.050
What kind of research are you doing?

00:10:57.050 --> 00:11:01.930
The easiest way to explain it is simply to show it in action.

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:04.850
Huh? What are these?

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:09.560
Those glass orbs are lamps that react to sound.

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:12.020
They basically act as hearts.

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:12.940
Oh?

00:11:13.310 --> 00:11:14.650
Let's see...

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:16.570
Let me demonstrate on this mouse.

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:19.570
I'll take those back, now.

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:20.950
Aww.

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:26.740
First I'll install the resonance lamp in the place where the heart goes.

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:31.670
Then, I'll connect the lamp to this specially-made bottle using a cord.

00:11:31.670 --> 00:11:32.830
And when I play it...

00:11:44.350 --> 00:11:46.220
Wow, that's awesome!

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:47.770
It's moving.

00:11:51.350 --> 00:11:53.190
Hey, it's stopped.

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:56.440
A mouse's heartbeat is too fast for me.

00:11:56.440 --> 00:12:00.110
So this is what's gotten George the turtle and that fish up and moving?

00:12:00.610 --> 00:12:06.870
Yes. The target of my research is "life."
These are the fruits of my labor.

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:08.870
George is quite the lazybones.

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:13.080
He just needs the beat of the fountain and the night dew to keep him going.

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:15.880
And the fish?

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:19.380
Hm... That one's a little special.

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:22.680
You'll notice how if you take another look.

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:30.140
It's so energetic.

00:12:30.140 --> 00:12:31.930
But really creepy.

00:12:31.930 --> 00:12:33.890
Not quite what I was referring to.

00:12:36.230 --> 00:12:38.690
There's no cord to transfer the sound.

00:12:38.690 --> 00:12:41.900
Precisely. He's wireless.

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:46.120
I found a way to attach a transmitter to a living creature

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:50.410
so that bones can use a remote, living heartbeat to power their movement.

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:54.370
I see. So where's that transmitter?

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:56.290
Uh, w-well...

00:12:56.710 --> 00:13:00.670
It was attached to a different fish that I caught in this marsh.

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:02.260
It swam away on you, didn't it?

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:04.050
Talk about sleeping on the job.

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:07.550
I-It was a very energetic fish!

00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:12.270
Without it, those bones could never move so powerfully through the water!

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:18.770
Hakumei!

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:25.280
I can't express how sorry I am.

00:13:27.110 --> 00:13:28.780
I should have been more careful with him.

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:31.290
You certainly should have!
Hakumei can't swim, you know!

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:34.620
A-Are you okay?

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:39.460
What is this?

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:42.300
This is... the transmitter.

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:43.420
What?

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:49.470
Now that I think about it, the day before yesterday when we ate that fish we caught in the swamp...

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:52.930
I bit into something strange.

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:54.270
Spit it out, then.

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:55.980
I swallowed it!

00:13:55.980 --> 00:13:56.600
Huh?

00:13:57.980 --> 00:14:00.270
So it was <i>your</i> heartbeat, then...

00:14:00.270 --> 00:14:02.730
That's why it was so peppy.

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:11.990
A package for you, miss!

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:13.830
Whoa, whoa...

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:15.950
Sign or seal, please.

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:20.380
Hakumei, we've got a package from Sen!

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:23.840
Wow, they're dark chub!

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:25.590
She said it's to apologize for the other day.

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:28.260
Hm? Something's stuck to it...

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:28.970
Huh?

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:42.980
<i>I look forward to doing more research with you. Best regards.</i>

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:59.330
Grinding coffee beans seems like such hard work.

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:02.000
Couldn't you get some that are already ground?

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:04.380
It tastes better if you do it yourself.

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:09.590
Home-roasted and home-ground is our motto.

00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:14.100
Speaking of the roast, did you change the beans?

00:15:16.390 --> 00:15:19.480
I didn't change them, but... you noticed a difference?

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:21.600
Yes. It still tastes good, though.

00:15:22.190 --> 00:15:24.310
I'm using a different mill.

00:15:24.310 --> 00:15:27.110
The one I've used forever is broken.

00:15:27.110 --> 00:15:28.740
Want me to fix it for you?

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:30.200
Can you do that?

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:32.110
Fixing things is what I do.

00:15:33.030 --> 00:15:35.200
Here it is. Think you're up to it?

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:39.200
What's the problem with it?

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:42.370
The handle. It just stopped turning.

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:45.380
Okay, I'll give it a try.

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:47.090
You're a lifesaver.

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:49.880
Does this mill mean a lot to you?

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:52.470
Yeah, it does.

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:59.140
Normally, what I drink and what you two drink is just about the only thing I use it for.

00:16:01.270 --> 00:16:06.610
Maybe it's just been showing its age.
Or maybe the previous owner rubbed off on it.

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:09.190
Either way, it produces an uneven grind.

00:16:09.190 --> 00:16:12.110
I can't really serve that to customers.

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:16.530
What? You don't consider us your customers?

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:19.660
Do you remember ever paying me for anything besides liquor?

00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:22.790
Thank you for always treating us.

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:23.710
No sweat.

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:30.800
There's no denying it, though.
The old owner sure made good coffee with this thing.

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:38.180
I'll be taking it to pieces, so I might not be able to put it all back together. Is that okay?

00:16:38.180 --> 00:16:40.180
Yeah, sure, sure.

00:16:40.890 --> 00:16:44.810
Well then, how about I grind some premium beans to cheer us all up?

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:45.900
Oh boy!

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:50.980
All right, analysis complete.

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:52.860
It's cleaner than I expected.

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:54.700
Yeah, it is.

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:59.200
The burr's still sharp.
Just enough that it hurts to touch.

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:04.540
So what did the last owner's coffee taste like?

00:17:05.870 --> 00:17:10.090
It was really tasty. Tasty with a gentle flavor.

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:16.430
But the woman herself was as far from gentle as it gets.

00:17:16.430 --> 00:17:22.100
Making it, or roasting it...
she didn't teach me a single thing.

00:17:22.770 --> 00:17:26.560
Then you learned how to make this coffee on your own?

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:27.650
I guess I did.

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:32.730
I bought my own mill, and I tried out many different things,

00:17:33.190 --> 00:17:36.860
but I still haven't reached her level.

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:39.280
Yours tastes really good, too.

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:41.870
Thanks for that.

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:48.880
I don't see any damaged parts.

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:54.590
I'll put it back together now. If it still doesn't work, that might be the end of it.

00:17:54.590 --> 00:17:55.880
Is that so?

00:17:56.430 --> 00:17:58.470
It happens sometimes.

00:17:58.470 --> 00:18:03.890
There's no problem, and then suddenly the thing stops working for no apparent reason.

00:18:04.470 --> 00:18:07.390
Doesn't that just mean it's broken?

00:18:07.390 --> 00:18:08.650
Not exactly.

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:12.150
"Broken" implies it can be fixed.

00:18:12.860 --> 00:18:17.650
I hate to say it, but in that situation all you can do is give up, have some liquor, and go to sleep.

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:19.660
I see!

00:18:20.370 --> 00:18:25.290
Then how about I put some sake on to warm?
I've got some good yellowtail to go with it.

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:27.960
Whoops—I wasn't trying to impose!

00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:33.920
All that's left is to tighten the top.

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:37.720
All done, but...

00:18:39.380 --> 00:18:40.680
It won't budge!

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:42.470
How mysterious.

00:18:42.470 --> 00:18:47.140
Maybe it's the center part. Should I try filing it down?

00:18:48.100 --> 00:18:52.650
Oh, no. You don't have to do all that. Thank you.

00:18:53.110 --> 00:18:56.280
Mikochi, will you take down the signboard for me?

00:18:57.610 --> 00:19:00.660
It's gotten late, so you should stay over.

00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:03.240
Understood. Thank you for that!

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:06.750
No problem. I'll take payment for the sake, though.

00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:33.860
Barkeep. Barkeep!

00:19:36.070 --> 00:19:38.360
What is it? Do you know what time it is?

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:39.400
This is amazing.

00:19:39.400 --> 00:19:41.280
Come over here, quietly.

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:46.280
What is it?

00:19:55.590 --> 00:19:57.300
It's a tsukumogami.

00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:03.300
They say that they're suddenly born of long-treasured tools.

00:20:23.110 --> 00:20:26.070
Hey, let me use the mill.

00:20:26.660 --> 00:20:31.370
No can do. This fella only responds to my touch.

00:20:31.370 --> 00:20:34.790
You'll need to find something that works on your own.

00:20:38.300 --> 00:20:43.180
Still, I so badly wanted to try out that mill.

00:20:56.730 --> 00:20:58.610
Thanks for your hard work.

00:21:01.070 --> 00:21:04.110
No wonder it wouldn't move.

00:21:05.570 --> 00:21:09.620
I guess it decided it was time to take a break.

00:21:13.410 --> 00:21:18.130
Just like Ma did when she handed this place over to me.

00:21:22.010 --> 00:21:23.630
Good grief.

00:21:23.630 --> 00:21:27.640
Couldn't it spare a thought for the poor owner who's got to run this place without it?

00:21:29.760 --> 00:21:33.100
Barkeep. Brew us some coffee, would you?

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:36.560
Now there's a good idea. I'm wide awake, anyway.

00:21:46.530 --> 00:21:48.070
Sorry for the wait.

00:21:48.070 --> 00:21:49.410
Thank you!

00:21:51.580 --> 00:21:52.490
Here you go.

00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:54.410
Thanks.

00:22:06.630 --> 00:22:07.930
Delicious.

00:22:27.320 --> 00:22:35.410
When the breeze is pleasant, let's eat outside

00:22:35.410 --> 00:22:43.210
The olives are fragrant this time of year

00:22:43.210 --> 00:22:47.220
And in the plum-colored sky,

00:22:47.220 --> 00:22:51.180
the stars twinkle and shine

00:22:51.180 --> 00:22:55.720
After we take in an easy breath,

00:22:55.720 --> 00:23:00.100
the banquet will begin!

00:23:00.100 --> 00:23:03.690
A freshly-made smoked cheese quiche,

00:23:03.690 --> 00:23:07.440
sockeye salmon wrapped in magnolia leaves

00:23:07.440 --> 00:23:11.360
Look, the whole world is rejoicing

00:23:11.360 --> 00:23:16.200
It's itching to dance with us

00:23:16.200 --> 00:23:20.170
And what drink might fit a night like this?

00:23:20.170 --> 00:23:24.130
How about something botanical with pepper in it?

00:23:24.130 --> 00:23:29.420
We could even catch the moon with our tiny hands

00:23:29.420 --> 00:23:32.970
At least, that's how we're feeling
